course: dictionary
lesson: 14648
title: Precision: being exact
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Precision means being very exact and careful, so that every small detail is right. «The clockmaker worked with great precision, setting each tiny wheel in its place.» The clues are great care and tiny wheels, so precision means doing something exactly and carefully.
explain: Precision also has a science meaning: it is how exact a measurement is. «The ruler showed the pencil was 14.3 centimetres long, to the nearest millimetre.» A ruler that shows millimetres has more precision than one that only shows centimetres, because it can show smaller details.
explain: Precision can also come before a noun, where it describes the thing. «She used precision tools to cut the tiny gears.» Here the tools are made to be very exact. Ask yourself: is this word describing the thing that comes after it?
fact: Precision means being very exact and careful.
fact: In maths and science, precision depends on how small the units are, such as metres compared with millimetres.
fact: 3.14159 is more precise than 3.14, because it uses more decimal places.
fact: Accurate means close to the true value, while precise means exact and repeatable.
fact: «Precision» can be a noun («with precision») or an adjective before a noun («precision tools»).
exercise: «The surgeon placed each stitch with precision.» What does precision mean here? | Being happy with the result | *Being very exact and careful | Being very fast and loud | Being tired and bored
exercise: «The scale measures to the nearest gram, so it has great precision.» What does precision mean in this sentence? | *How exact a measurement is | How many people use the scale | How heavy the scale is | How long the scale takes to use
exercise: Which word in «She used precision tools to cut the tiny gears.» is an adjective that describes the tools? | tiny | gears | cut | *precision
test: «The answer 3.14159 is more precise than 3.14.» Why is it more precise? | It is bigger on the page | *It has more decimal places, so it is more exact | It is longer to read aloud | It is written in red ink
test: Which word means close to the true value? | Careless | Repeated | Precise | *Accurate
exam: Mina says precision and accuracy mean exactly the same thing. What is the best answer? | Yes, they mean exactly the same, so there is no difference | Accuracy is a type of colour | Precision means being loud and fast | *Not quite: accurate means close to the true value, while precise means exact and repeatable
